  "reasoning": "The patient presents with high fever, shivering/chills, and rashes on the arms and neck. High fever with chills suggests a systemic infection. The presence of rashes significantly narrows the differential diagnosis. Comparing with the provided examples, Dengue is strongly associated with fever accompanied by skin rashes or red spots on various body parts including arms and legs. Other conditions like Malaria typically lack prominent rashes, Chicken Pox presents with blisters rather than flat rashes, and Impetigo focuses on facial sores. Therefore, the symptom profile best matches Dengue.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]dengue[/DIAGNOSIS]"
}
